---
title: Boston Baked Beans
author: Shirley Simmonds
servings: 8
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 4.5 hours
---

Place the @haricot beans{450%g} in a large #pan{} and cover with @water{1.2%litres}. Cover and simmer for ~{45%minutes} until almost cooked. Drain, reserving @bean water{300%ml}.

Chop the @onion{2}(peeled) with the @cloves{4} and place them in the bottom of a #casserole dish{3.5%litres}. Score the rind of the @pickled pork{225%g} or @green streaky bacon{} and place it in the dish with the beans, @black treacle{3%tbsp}, @dark soft brown sugar{75%g}, @English mustard{2%tsp}, and @salt{2%tsp}.

Chop the @onion{2} and place in the bottom of a #casserole dish{3.5%litres}. Add the beans, @smoked tofu, cubed{225%g}, @black treacle{3%tbsp}, @dark soft brown sugar{75%g}, @English mustard{2%tsp}, @ground cloves{1%tsp}, and @soy sauce{2%tbsp}. Pour over the reserved bean water.

Cover and cook in a 150°C oven for ~{3%hours}, removing the lid for the last ~{30%minutes} if the mixture is still wet.

> Serve with fresh crusty bread and a green salad.
